---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Javier Cruz Galera: Performance marketing, in the open."
  description="Practitioner writing on performance marketing reporting, A/B testing, and operational workflows, plus an open SEO/GEO experiment tracking how this site ranks and gets cited."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-8">
        Performance marketing, in the open.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        Most of what I know about performance marketing I did not figure out alone (aside from
        countless hours of research, and online courses). I had managers and senior operators who
        were generous with their time and ruthless with their feedback. They taught me that the
        work is only as good as the decision it changes, and that a test you cannot defend is not
        really a test. This site is me writing those lessons down and passing them forward.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href="/playbooks"
          class="bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-medium hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors"
        >
          Read the Playbooks
        </a>
        <a
          href="/lab-notes"
          class="border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-medium hover:border-gray-400 hover:text-gray-900 transition-colors"
        >
          See the Lab Notes
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What this site is -->
  <section class="border-y border-gray-100 bg-gray-50 py-16" aria-labelledby="about-site-heading">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 id="about-site-heading" class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest mb-10">
        What this site is
      </h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-10">

        <article>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">The craft</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Dashboards and reporting that drive decisions, not just describe what happened.
            A/B testing done in a way you can actually defend. The operational workflows behind
            the numbers. These are the parts of performance marketing nobody writes about honestly.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/playbooks"
            class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors"
          >
            Read the playbooks →
          </a>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">The lab</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            This site is the experiment. Every post is optimized with a real hypothesis.
            Rankings, traffic, and AI-engine visibility are tracked. Results are posted openly
            in Lab Notes, including the things that don't work.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/lab-notes"
            class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors"
          >
            See the lab notes →
          </a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
